id: pm-7wzb6d
title: "GH-1184: scalar merge conflict ordering ignores recency and requested preference"
description: "On pm 2026.9.3, same-field scalar conflicts converge by lexicographic stable_value_order. This preserves direction independence but can retain an older status or priority solely because its serialized spelling sorts first, while --prefer ours|theirs is recorded yet does not affect the result. The report proposes a direction-independent recency key with an explicit deterministic tie-break, or a truthful narrowing of the --prefer contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-03T18:06:36.495Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T09:23:02.656Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T06:43:08.816Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T06:43:08.816Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Both merge directions converge to the same scalar value; the ordering key is declared and uses meaningful recorded evidence rather than spelling; --prefer behavior and exclusions are machine-readable and match help; status and priority regressions cover older/newer writes, equal timestamps, both directions, and both preference values; receipts remain truthful and privacy-safe"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: pm-cli 2026.9.3; Node 26.5.0; Linux; fresh merge-driver install
repro_steps: "Create one item, diverge two branches, update the same scalar at different timestamps, then merge in both directions with default, --prefer ours, and --prefer theirs; observe the same lexicographically smaller value retained."
resolution: "Item scalar conflicts now use whole-document updated_at recency, stable value ordering only for timestamp ties, and expose retained_side, resolution_basis, and requested_preference_applied through the public SDK and receipts."
expected_result: Both merge directions converge using meaningful recorded recency evidence; equal timestamps remain deterministic; preference exclusions are explicit and machine-readable.
actual_result: "Focused direction tests, full 8,351-test exact coverage, complete static quality, and packed CLI/SDK acceptance all passed."
component: sdk/merge
