comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T18:06:36.495Z","harness:codex","GitHub source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1184. All-status duplicate check searched scalar merge, stable value order, preference, recency, and direction lineages; pm-qckpnq closed the truthful requested_preference receipt field and pm-dlx7v7 closed direction independence, but neither makes the winning scalar policy recency-aware. This is new recurrence/semantic-policy work, linked rather than reopening shipped history."
  "2026-09-03T18:07:08.462Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage comment: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1184#issuecomment-5530007441"
  "2026-09-04T05:49:52.341Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: scalar conflicts now use whole-document metadata.updated_at recency, retain a deterministic stable-value tie break when timestamps match, and record retained_side plus resolution_basis in SDK decisions. Requested ours/theirs is explicitly reported as not applied for the item merge driver, preventing a misleading preference claim. Directional tests prove both merge directions converge on the newer document."
  "2026-09-04T06:23:32.475Z","harness:codex","Final repository verification: pnpm quality:static passed the complete mandatory static gate; node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage passed 603 files and 8,350 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; pnpm security:scan, pnpm audit, documentation links, and package-artifact checks passed. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alert inventories were empty. Focused merge-direction contract tests passed."
  "2026-09-04T06:42:48.525Z","harness:codex","Terminal closeout evidence: exact-tree coverage passed 603 files and 8,351 tests at 100/100/100/100; the complete exact-tree static-quality pipeline passed all repository, SDK-surface, token, graph, and append-only history ratchets."
  "2026-09-04T07:42:09.787Z","harness:codex","Review round 1: CodeRabbit identified that absent scalar values were omitted by JSON.stringify and collided with the literal string undefined in canonical hashing. Added the public JSON-stable missing-value marker and shared evidence hash primitive across merge results, receipts, driver snapshots, and repair verification, with a later-deletion regression."
  "2026-09-04T08:19:57.940Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit identified missing-scalar omission and hash collision risk. Implemented public JSON-stable absence encoding plus one shared hash primitive across three-way decisions, driver field hashes, durable summaries, and history-repair verification. Negative controls cover every rejected marker shape and literal string undefined. Exact gate: 603 files, 8,352 tests, 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-09-04T09:23:02.656Z","harness:codex","Review round 2 evidence: present and missing scalar values now occupy disjoint hash domains, the serialized missing marker is reserved at item-merge input, and all driver/reconciliation fixtures consume the shared public hash primitive. Negative controls prove a present marker-shaped object cannot impersonate deletion."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T06:22:41.873Z","harness:codex",Caller-relative merge preference cannot provide direction-independent convergence for scalar conflicts; whole-document updated_at recency with stable value ordering on ties does.
